  "notes": "A German tropical-house producer named in the genre documentation as one of the figures who established the style as a trend. The kit is the entry's and it is the most percussion-forward reading in this section: \"soft deep-house kick, clap on 2&4, offbeat shaker, bongos and steel percussion in place of a hat bed\", so the hat fill density falls to 0.12 — the lowest here — and a four-lane bongo/shaker/woodblock/triangle bed runs 5-8 hits a bar at -2 dB. \"Hardly any big drops\" and an arrangement \"relaxed and chill by design\" is the ladder off, low drop-out and fills pushed to every 8 and 16 bars. The lead palette is the documented one — \"flutes, folk guitars, horns, steel drums, marimbas\" combined with lush pads and an occasional edgy synth — and the melodic material is pentatonic over major and modal-major four-chord loops, with the harmony inherited from the source song on the remix-derived records `[LOW-CONF]`, a mark repeated here. The instrumental break restating the hook is the standard device, so every structure places a bridge after a hook. Bass is \"round, soft syncopated sub\". ⚠ The research states that all parameters are sub-genre convention; that mark is repeated here, and every number above is INFERRED.",
